1 GOSUB

   Runs the commands at a label of the same command procedure, at the
   same command level, until a RETURN comes back to the command after
   the GOSUB.

   Format

     GOSUB label

2 Parameter

 label

   Where the subroutine starts, found as GOTO finds a label.

2 Description

   The commands GOSUB runs see the procedure's labels and local symbols:
   they are at its command level.  GOSUBs may be nested 15 deep.  A
   label that isn't found ends the procedure (DCL-W-USGOSUB).  See
   RETURN for the status.

2 Examples

   1.$ GOSUB SHOW_COUNT
     $ EXIT
     $ SHOW_COUNT:
     $ SHOW SYMBOL COUNT
     $ RETURN

     Shows COUNT, then exits.
